                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "in_1763096020270_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert at analyzing compensation plan documents. Extract detailed information about this specific component.\n\nCOMPONENT NAME: {{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\n\nSLICED CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.SLICE_FOR_COMPONENT.$output.result}}\n\nLOOKUP CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.lookupContextText}}\nSupported payout frequency values for this org: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.payoutFrequencyValues}}\nSupported reset interval values for this org: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.resetIntervalValues}}\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\nExtract the following details for the \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\" component.\nUse the COMPONENT SECTION inside the SLICED CONTEXT for component-specific facts. Use PLAN CONTEXT only for shared rules and definitions.\n\n1. Component Name\n   - Verify the exact name as stated in the document\n   - May refine if more complete name is found in detail sections\n   - Preserve original capitalization and punctuation\n\n2. Component Type\n\n   - Use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT `componentTypeAllowed`\n\n   BONUS: Performance bonuses\n   - Quarterly, semi-annual, or annual bonuses\n   - Tiered bonuses with performance thresholds\n   - Accelerator bonuses\n   - Performance multiplier bonuses\n\n   COMMISSION: Transaction-based commission\n   - Per-deal commission\n   - Revenue-based commission\n   - Variable rate commission structures\n   - Per-transaction payouts\n\n   STANDARD: Standard compensation components\n   - Base salary components\n   - Fixed incentive components\n   - Other standard compensation elements\n\n3. Incentive Type (optional)\n\n   - Use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT `incentiveTypeAllowed`\n   - Usually COMMISSION for transaction/event-oriented components\n   - Usually BONUS for interval/bonus-oriented components\n   - Use null for STANDARD components or when not inferable\n\n4. Payout Frequency (optional, interval components only)\n\n   - Return exactly one of the supported payout frequency values for this org, or null\n   - Choose the closest org-supported interval implied by the BRD\n   - Prefer a supported value over null whenever the BRD gives any periodic cadence evidence for the component, measures, goals, or payout timing\n   - Examples:\n     * \"monthly bonus\", \"paid each period\" -> use the period-like supported value\n     * \"quarterly bonus\", \"Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4\" -> use the quarter-like supported value\n     * \"annual bonus\", \"year-end payout\", \"yearly\" -> use the year-like supported value\n     * \"semi-annual\", \"half-yearly\", \"twice a year\" -> use the semi-annual supported value when present\n     * annual goal / annual target cadence for the component -> use the year-like supported value when no better payout cadence is stated\n     * quarter goal / quarterly target cadence for the component -> use the quarter-like supported value when no better payout cadence is stated\n\n   null:\n   - Use null only when the component is clearly transaction/event driven and no periodic cadence evidence exists anywhere in the component context\n\n5. Description\n   - Comprehensive description of what this component is and how it works\n   - Include key characteristics:\n     * What is measured\n     * How it's calculated (high level)\n     * When it's paid\n     * What behavior it incentivizes\n   - 2-4 sentences recommended\n\n6. Effective Dates (optional)\n   - Extract component startDate and endDate only when the component has its own explicit effective window\n   - Use YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - If the BRD only gives plan-level dates or shared dates, set component startDate and endDate to null\n   - Do not infer component dates from plan dates\n\n7. Target Incentive Percent\n   - Extract the component's percentage allocation of plan target incentive\n   - Examples: \"60% weight\", \"40% allocation\", \"component influence is 25%\"\n   - Return as numeric value without % symbol\n   - If not explicitly stated, set to null\n\n8. Confidence (extraction quality indicator)\n   - Rate your confidence in this extraction on a scale of 0.0 to 1.0\n   - 1.0 = Complete information explicitly stated\n   - 0.8 = Most information found, minor inference\n   - 0.6 = Partial information, significant inference\n   - 0.4 = Limited information, substantial inference\n   - 0.2 = Minimal information, mostly inference\n\n9. Split Option (component-level tier behavior)\n   - Extract ONLY when BRD explicitly states split behavior\n   - Allowed values: NONE, NON_PROPORTIONAL, PROPORTIONAL\n   - Map language examples:\n     * \"single rate\", \"no split\", \"flat rate\" -> NONE\n     * \"step rates\", \"discrete tiers\", \"fixed rate per tier\" -> NON_PROPORTIONAL\n     * \"interpolated\", \"pro-rated\", \"sliding scale\" -> PROPORTIONAL\n   - If split behavior is not explicitly stated, set to null\n\n\n10. Include Indirect Credits (optional)\n     - Type of indirect credits to include in calculation\n     - Use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT `includeIndirectCreditsAllowed`\n     - Map language examples:\n       * \"no rollup\", individual rep only -> NONE\n       * \"all indirect credits\", \"team + manager\" -> ALL\n       * \"management override\", \"manager rollup\", \"rollup credits\" -> MGR\n       * \"team credits only\", \"team bonus\" -> TEAM\n     - If not stated, set to null (deployment may default later)\n\n11. True Up (optional)\n    - Whether earnings are calculated cumulatively\n    - true when BRD mentions \"true-up\", \"cumulative earnings\", \"year-to-date recalculation\", \"running total adjustment\"\n    - false when explicitly non-cumulative\n    - null when not stated\n\n12. Reset Interval (optional, only if trueUp is true)\n    - Span of time for cumulative calculation reset\n    - Return exactly one of the supported reset interval values for this org, or null\n    - Example: \"quarterly true-up\" -> trueUp=true, resetInterval=<quarter-like supported value>\n    - If trueUp is null/false, resetInterval must be null\nClassification Guidelines:\n- \"Bonus\" in name → BONUS\n- \"Commission\" in name → COMMISSION\n- \"Base\", \"Salary\", or \"Fixed\" components → STANDARD\n- Period-based (quarterly, annual) with goal attainment → Usually BONUS\n- Per-transaction or per-deal → Usually COMMISSION\n- Tied to achievement percentage (95%, 110%, etc.) → Usually BONUS\n- Tied to transaction value → Usually COMMISSION\n- Fixed compensation, non-variable pay → Usually STANDARD\n\nPayout Frequency Guidelines:\n- \"monthly\" -> choose the period-like supported value\n- \"quarterly\", \"Q1\", \"each quarter\" -> choose the quarter-like supported value\n- \"semi-annual\", \"bi-annual\", \"half-yearly\" -> choose the semi-annual supported value when present\n- \"annual\", \"year-end\", \"yearly\", \"FY2025\" -> choose the year-like supported value\n- \"per deal\", \"per transaction\", \"on each sale\" → null (event-driven cadence)\n\nFocus only on information related to \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\". Be conservative and precise.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON matching this exact schema:\n\n{\n  \"componentName\": \"string (required) - Exact component name\",\n  \"componentType\": \"string (required) - exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT componentTypeAllowed\",\n  \"incentiveType\": \"string or null - exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT incentiveTypeAllowed\",\n  \"payoutFrequency\": \"string or null - exact value from the supported payout frequency values for this org\",\n  \"description\": \"string or null - Detailed description of the component\",\n  \"startDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null - Component effective start date when explicitly stated\",\n  \"endDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null - Component effective end date when explicitly stated\",\n  \"targetIncentivePercent\": \"number (0-100) or null - Component allocation of plan target incentive\",\n  \"splitOption\": \"NONE | NON_PROPORTIONAL | PROPORTIONAL | null - Component tier split behavior\",\n  \"includeIndirectCredits\": \"string or null - exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT includeIndirectCreditsAllowed\",\n  \"trueUp\": \"boolean or null - Whether earnings are calculated cumulatively\",\n  \"resetInterval\": \"string or null - exact value from the supported reset interval values for this org for cumulative reset span (only if trueUp=true)\",\n  \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required) - Confidence in extraction quality\"\n}\n\nIMPORTANT REMINDERS:\n- Respond with ONLY the JSON object, no additional text\n- Focus exclusively on \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\" - ignore other components\n- componentType must be an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT componentTypeAllowed\n- incentiveType must be null or an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT incentiveTypeAllowed\n- payoutFrequency must be null or exactly one of the supported payout frequency values for this org\n- Prefer the closest supported payout frequency value over null whenever the document provides any usable cadence evidence\n- startDate and endDate must be null unless the component has its own explicit effective dates\n- targetIncentivePercent is numeric without % symbol\n- splitOption must be null unless explicitly stated by BRD language\n- includeIndirectCredits must be null unless BRD mentions rollup/team/manager credits; when present use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT includeIndirectCreditsAllowed\n- resetInterval must be null unless trueUp is true, and when present it must be exactly one of the supported reset interval values for this org\n- Use null for any field where information is not clearly stated\n- Preserve exact component name from document"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"componentName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Exact name of the component\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"componentType\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"BONUS\", \"COMMISSION\", \"STANDARD\"], \"description\": \"Type of component\"}, \"incentiveType\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"COMMISSION\", \"BONUS\", null], \"description\": \"IC incentive type. COMMISSION is per-event and BONUS is per-interval.\"}, \"payoutFrequency\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Formula payout cadence when component is interval-based; expected to match an org interval value from lookup context\"}, \"description\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Detailed description of the component\"}, \"startDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Component effective start date in YYYY-MM-DD format when explicitly stated\"}, \"endDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Component effective end date in YYYY-MM-DD format when explicitly stated\"}, \"targetIncentivePercent\": {\"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100, \"description\": \"Percent allocation of plan target incentive for this component\"}, \"splitOption\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"NONE\", \"NON_PROPORTIONAL\", \"PROPORTIONAL\", null], \"description\": \"Optional component-level split behavior when explicitly stated\"}, \"includeIndirectCredits\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"NONE\", \"ALL\", \"MGR\", \"TEAM\", null], \"description\": \"Type of indirect credits to include in component calculation\"}, \"trueUp\": {\"type\": [\"boolean\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Whether earnings are calculated cumulatively (true-up)\"}, \"resetInterval\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Reset span for cumulative calculation, only valid when trueUp is true; expected to match an org interval value from lookup context\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for extraction quality\"}}, \"required\": [\"componentName\", \"componentType\", \"confidence\"], \"allOf\": [{\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"trueUp\": {\"const\": true}}, \"required\": [\"trueUp\"]}, \"then\": {\"properties\": {\"resetInterval\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}}}, \"else\": {\"properties\": {\"resetInterval\": {\"type\": \"null\"}}}}], \"additionalProperties\": false}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "code": "PC_MEASURE_EXTRACTOR",
                  "id": "1763096189967",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "PC Measure Extractor",
                    "reasoningEffort": "low",
                    "position": {
                      "x": 300,
                      "y": 200
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1763096850000"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "in_1763096189967_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert at analyzing compensation plan documents. Extract all performance measures for the \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\" component.\n\nCOMPONENT: {{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\n\nSLICED CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.SLICE_FOR_COMPONENT.$output.result}}\n\nLOOKUP CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.lookupContextText}}\nSupported performance interval values for this org: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.performanceIntervalValues}}\n\nSCOPE:\n\n- Extract measure-level facts only for this component.\n- This node does NOT decide scorecard vs component-level rate table usage. That is handled by RATE_TABLE_WIRING.\n- Focus on extraction with evidence from the COMPONENT SECTION inside the SLICED CONTEXT. Use PLAN CONTEXT only for shared rules.\n\nFor each measure, extract:\n\n1. Measure Name\n- Use source terminology.\n\n2. Description\n- 1-3 concise sentences.\n\n3. Measure Type (context-only classification)\n- REVENUE | QUOTA | ATTAINMENT | CUSTOM\n\n4. Unit of Measure\n- Prefer exact codes from LOOKUP CONTEXT `commissionUnitAllowed` when the measure is monetary or percentage based\n- QUANTITY and SCORE remain valid parser-only values for non-monetary measures\n\n5. Process Transaction\n- Use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT `processTransactionAllowed`\n\n6. Measure Split Option (optional)\n- NONE | NON_PROPORTIONAL | PROPORTIONAL | null\n- Extract only when explicitly stated for the measure\n\n7. Running Total Flag (optional)\n- true when BRD indicates cumulative/running total logic for measure attainment\n- false when explicitly non-cumulative\n- null when not stated\n\n8. Weight (optional)\n- Percentage influence this measure has on the component\n- Examples: \"60% weight\", \"weighted at 40%\", \"20% allocation\"\n- Return as integer without % symbol\n- Multiple measures in a component should total 100%\n- If not stated and only one measure exists, assume 100\n- If not stated with multiple measures, set null\n\n9. Performance Interval (optional)\n- How often the measure resets its accumulated value\n- Return exactly one of the supported performance interval values for this org, or null\n- Examples:\n  - monthly or generic period cadence -> use the period-like supported value\n  - quarterly cadence -> use the quarter-like supported value\n  - semi-annual cadence -> use the semi-annual supported value when present\n  - annual or year-end cadence -> use the year-like supported value\n- If not explicitly stated, set null\n\n10. Measure Effective Dates (optional)\n- Extract measure-level effective start and end dates only when the BRD clearly states dates for the measure itself\n- Use YYYY-MM-DD format\n- If not explicitly stated for the measure, set startDate and endDate to null\n- Do not infer from plan dates, component dates, goal dates, or scorecard dates in this node\n\n11. Goals (target values, not payout tiers)\n- Fields: targetAmount, targetUnitOfMeasure, periodType, periodNumber, distributeEvenlyFlag, startDate, endDate, confidence\n- targetUnitOfMeasure values: AMOUNT or QUANTITY (null if not specified)\n- periodType values: Annual | Quarter | Period\n\n12. Measure Formula\n\n- Extract formulas that calculate measure output, not component payout.\n- Accept explicit formula text or clear prose that defines the calculation.\n- ALWAYS include a concise business-friendly description of what the formula calculates.\n- Extract: formulaName, expression, description, variables, referencedRateTables, confidence, evidence\n- Formula `description` rules:\n  - required for every measure formula\n  - 1-2 concise business-facing sentences\n  - explain what the measure result represents and the high-level logic used to derive it\n  - use business language, not parser terminology or JSON field names\n  - if the BRD is sparse, infer a reasonable business summary from the extracted formula and measure context\n- TERMINAL LOOKUP INFERENCE:\n  - If a measure-owned scorecard or rate table is described as returning the measure result directly, and no additional arithmetic is described after the lookup, you may infer a standalone lookup expression.\n  - A bare lookup alias such as `Rate Table Rate` or `RTR` is acceptable.\n  - Brief descriptive lookup phrasing is also acceptable when it clearly means only the standalone lookup result.\n  - Keep standalone lookup expressions concise and avoid long narrative prose in `expression`.\n  - Do not invent identity math such as `1 * Rate Table Rate` unless the document explicitly states multiplication or another operator.\n  - If the document says the looked-up value is multiplied, weighted, capped, summed, or otherwise combined with another operand, include that math explicitly instead of collapsing it to a standalone lookup expression.\n  - If it is unclear whether the lookup result is the final measure result or only an intermediate factor, lower confidence and add evidence rather than forcing a standalone lookup expression.\n- Examples:\n  - If the BRD says the returned scorecard value becomes the measure result directly, `expression` may be a bare lookup alias or a concise standalone lookup phrase.\n  - If the BRD says the looked-up value is multiplied by another operand, return the full math explicitly and do NOT collapse to a standalone lookup expression.\n- `variables` must include only operands explicitly referenced by the returned formula expression.\n- Do not include scorecard or rate-table driver attributes unless they appear directly in the formula expression itself.\n- If the formula is only a standalone rate-table lookup, return `variables: []`.\n- Treat `expression` as draft business-visible formula wording for resolver handoff, not the final canonical token stream.\n- referencedRateTables must use rate table names exactly as stated in the document/extracted context. Do not invent standardized names.\n\n13. Credit Categories (at least one per measure)\n\n- Extract all explicitly eligible categories feeding the measure.\n- One category per item; do not group multiple categories.\n- Avoid incomplete umbrella outputs like \"etc.\" or \"and others\".\n- Extract: categoryName, description, confidence, evidence\n\n14. Confidence\n- 0.0 to 1.0 for measure/formula/category records.\n\nCROSS-FIELD BUSINESS RULES (important guidance):\n\n- If the parent component is COMMISSION type, processTransaction should usually be INDIVIDUAL (per-transaction earnings)\n- If the parent component is BONUS type, processTransaction should usually be GROUP (aggregated per interval)\n- When processTransaction is INDIVIDUAL, all measures with earning basis in the same component must share the same credit category\n- These are guidelines not absolutes — defer to explicit BRD language when it contradicts\n\nEVIDENCE RULES:\n\n- Include short source snippets in `evidence` fields.\n- Keep evidence concise and verbatim-like; do not paraphrase aggressively.\n- If confidence is below 0.7, evidence is mandatory.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON:\n\n{\n  \"measures\": [\n    {\n      \"measureName\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"description\": \"string or null\",\n      \"measureType\": \"REVENUE | QUOTA | ATTAINMENT | CUSTOM (optional context)\",\n      \"unitOfMeasure\": \"string (required) - prefer LOOKUP CONTEXT commissionUnitAllowed; QUANTITY and SCORE also allowed when applicable\",\n      \"processTransaction\": \"string (required) - exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT processTransactionAllowed\",\n      \"splitOption\": \"NONE | NON_PROPORTIONAL | PROPORTIONAL | null\",\n      \"runningTotalFlag\": \"boolean or null\",\n      \"weight\": \"integer (0-100) or null - measure weight as percentage\",\n      \"performanceInterval\": \"string or null - exact value from the supported performance interval values for this org for measure reset interval\",\n      \"startDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null - measure effective start date when explicitly stated\",\n      \"endDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null - measure effective end date when explicitly stated\",\n      \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required)\",\n      \"goals\": [...],\n      \"formula\": {\n        \"formulaName\": \"string (required)\",\n        \"expression\": \"string (required)\",\n        \"description\": \"string (required) - 1-2 business-friendly sentences explaining what the measure formula calculates\",\n        \"variables\": [\"array of strings\"],\n        \"referencedRateTables\": [\"array of strings\"],\n        \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required)\",\n        \"evidence\": \"string (required)\"\n      },\n      \"creditCategories\": [\n        {\n          \"categoryName\": \"string (required)\",\n          \"description\": \"string or null\",\n          \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required)\",\n          \"evidence\": \"string (required)\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Only extract measures that are clearly defined in the BRD and have either an explicit calculation or a clearly stated pass-through basis.\n- Goals array may be empty if no targets are specified.\n- Do not perform cross-layer disambiguation here.\n- Keep splitOption/runningTotalFlag as null unless the BRD states them clearly.\n- performanceInterval must be null or exactly one of the supported performance interval values for this org.\n- Never return `null` or an empty string for `formula.description`.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON with no markdown."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"measures\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"measureName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the performance measure\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"description\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Description of what the measure represents\"}, \"measureType\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"REVENUE\", \"QUOTA\", \"ATTAINMENT\", \"CUSTOM\"], \"description\": \"Type of measure\"}, \"unitOfMeasure\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"AMOUNT\", \"PERCENT\", \"QUANTITY\", \"SCORE\"], \"description\": \"Unit of measurement\"}, \"processTransaction\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"INDIVIDUAL\", \"GROUP\"], \"description\": \"How transactions are processed\"}, \"splitOption\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"NONE\", \"NON_PROPORTIONAL\", \"PROPORTIONAL\", null], \"description\": \"Optional measure-level split behavior\"}, \"runningTotalFlag\": {\"type\": [\"boolean\", \"null\"], \"default\": false, \"description\": \"Whether the measure uses cumulative running total\"}, \"weight\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100, \"description\": \"Percentage influence this measure has on the component (total should be 100)\"}, \"performanceInterval\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"How often the measure resets its accumulated value; expected to match an org interval value from lookup context\"}, \"startDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\", \"description\": \"Measure start date in YYYY-MM-DD format\"}, \"endDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\", \"description\": \"Measure end date in YYYY-MM-DD format\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for measure extraction quality\"}, \"goals\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"targetAmount\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"description\": \"Target value for the goal\"}, \"targetUnitOfMeasure\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"AMOUNT\", \"QUANTITY\", null], \"description\": \"Unit of measure for the goal target\"}, \"periodType\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"Annual\", \"Quarter\", \"Period\"], \"description\": \"Type of period\"}, \"periodNumber\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 1, \"description\": \"Period number\"}, \"distributeEvenlyFlag\": {\"type\": [\"boolean\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Whether the goal should be distributed evenly\"}, \"startDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\", \"description\": \"Goal start date in YYYY-MM-DD format\"}, \"endDate\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\", \"description\": \"Goal end date in YYYY-MM-DD format\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for goal extraction quality\"}}, \"required\": [\"targetAmount\", \"periodType\", \"confidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"formula\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"description\": \"Formula to calculate the measure result (REQUIRED - 1:1 with measure)\", \"properties\": {\"formulaName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the formula\"}, \"expression\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Draft business-visible formula wording for resolver handoff, using {variables} where helpful\"}, \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Business-friendly summary of what this formula calculates\"}, \"variables\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Variables used in the formula\"}, \"referencedRateTables\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Exact observed rate table names referenced in the draft formula wording\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet for the extracted formula\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0}}, \"required\": [\"formulaName\", \"expression\", \"description\", \"variables\", \"evidence\", \"confidence\"]}, \"creditCategories\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"description\": \"Credit categories that feed this measure (REQUIRED - at least one)\", \"minItems\": 1, \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"categoryName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the credit category\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"description\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Description of what credits this category captures\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet for this credit category\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for credit category extraction\"}}, \"required\": [\"categoryName\", \"evidence\", \"confidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}, \"required\": [\"measureName\", \"unitOfMeasure\", \"processTransaction\", \"confidence\", \"goals\", \"formula\", \"creditCategories\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}, \"required\": [\"measures\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "code": "RATE_TABLE_EXTRACTOR",
                  "id": "1763096395577",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Rate Table Extractor",
                    "reasoningEffort": "low",
                    "position": {
                      "x": 300,
                      "y": 300
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1763096850000"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "in_1763096395577_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert at analyzing compensation plan documents and extracting rate tables. Extract all rate tables for the \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\" component.\n\nCOMPONENT: {{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\n\nSLICED CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.SLICE_FOR_COMPONENT.$output.result}}\n\nLOOKUP CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LOOKUP_CONTEXT.$output.result.lookupContextText}}\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\nRate tables define lookup outputs based on one or more dimensions. They can be used to determine measure results, scorecard outputs, multipliers, fixed amounts, or payout rates. Focus ONLY on rate tables related to \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\".\nPrioritize extraction from the COMPONENT SECTION inside the SLICED CONTEXT. Use PLAN CONTEXT only for shared policies or terminology.\n\nLook for rate tables in the document in various formats:\n- Structured tables (ASCII, markdown, or formatted text)\n- Tier descriptions with ranges and rates (e.g., \"Below 95%: 0%, 95-110%: 100%\")\n- Natural language prose descriptions (e.g., \"Up to 10,000 earns 2.5%, from 10,000 to 20,000 earns 4%\")\n- Achievement scorecards or driver tables that convert an input into a measure result or scored value\n- Commission schedules\n- Payout matrices\n\nWHAT TO EXTRACT AS RATE TABLES:\n\n=== PRESCRIPTIVE vs ILLUSTRATIVE TABLES (CRITICAL) ===\n\nEXTRACT as rate tables:\n- Tables that DEFINE the calculation rules (\"The bonus rate is determined by...\")\n- Tables introduced with prescriptive language (\"rates are\", \"payout schedule\", \"commission structure\")\n- Tables introduced as scorecards, achievement tables, driver tables, lookup bands, or similar named lookup structures\n- Tables that show tier ranges with corresponding rates that WILL BE APPLIED\n\nDO NOT EXTRACT as rate tables:\n- Example/walkthrough tables showing sample calculations (\"Example:\", \"For instance:\", \"Walkthrough:\")\n- Tables that ILLUSTRATE how a formula works with specific numbers\n- Tables in sections titled \"Example Calculation\", \"Sample Payout\", \"Illustration\"\n- Tables that show input values and resulting outputs from a LINEAR FORMULA (no tiers)\n\nKEY DISTINCTION:\n- If the document says \"Monthly Bonus = Attainment × Target\" (linear formula with NO tiers), \n  then any table showing attainment→bonus pairs is ILLUSTRATIVE, not a rate table\n- If the document describes tiered/progressive rates (\"Below X: rate A, X to Y: rate B\"),\n  then extract as a rate table\n\n*** INPUT ADHERENCE RULE (CRITICAL) ***\n- Extract ONLY tiers/rates explicitly stated in the document\n- Do NOT add, infer, or extrapolate additional tiers beyond what is written\n- If document shows 3 tiers, output exactly 3 tiers - no more, no less\n- Do NOT assume open-ended ranges (e.g., \"and above\") unless explicitly stated\n- Each rate value in output must correspond to a rate explicitly provided in the document\n- If the calculation is LINEAR (no tiers), return empty rateTables array\n\nFor each rate table:\n\n1. rateTableName - Descriptive name for the table\n\n2. description - What this table determines\n\n3. rateTableType (determine what type of values are in the rate column):\n   - Use an exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT `commissionUnitAllowed`\n   - PERCENT: If rate values are percentages (2.5%, 100%, 150%)\n   - AMOUNT: If rate values are dollar amounts ($500, $1000)\n   \n   *** CRITICAL: Rate Table Type is determined by the RATE VALUES, NOT by dimension types ***\n   - A table with PERCENT dimensions (0-95%, 95-110%) can have AMOUNT rate type if rates are dollars\n   - A table with AMOUNT dimensions ($0-$10K, $10K-$50K) can have PERCENT rate type if rates are percentages\n   - Look at the PAYOUT column to determine type, not the tier/range column\n\n4. dimensions (array of dimension objects)\n   - Each dimension has:\n     * dimensionName: Name of the dimension\n     * dimensionType: RANGE, LIST, or TEXT\n     * dimensionSequence: 1 for first dimension, 2 for second\n      * unitOfMeasure: prefer exact codes from LOOKUP CONTEXT `commissionUnitAllowed`; STRING and EXPRESSION remain parser-only values when needed\n     * values: Array of string values\n     * tiers: OPTIONAL for RANGE dimensions. Preferred machine-readable normalized tier bounds.\n       - For numeric ranges, emit one tier per interval using numeric fields:\n         * minimumAmount: number\n         * maximumAmount: number\n       - Strip thousands separators from numeric bounds.\n       - Example: source `4,000 - 8,000` -> `{\"minimumAmount\": 4000, \"maximumAmount\": 8000}`\n       - If the range is textual/non-numeric, use `stringValue`\n     * inputExpression: Variable that feeds this dimension - MUST preserve the business identity of the source value\n        \n      *** INPUT EXPRESSION RULE (CRITICAL) ***\n      Use a canonical variable name that preserves WHICH measure or attribute feeds the dimension.\n      NEVER collapse distinct measure-result bindings to a bare generic variable when the document names the source measure.\n      \n      | Tier Based On | WRONG | CORRECT |\n      |---------------|-------|---------|\n      | Attainment % | {attainmentPercent} | {eligibleRevenueOutputAchieved} / {eligibleRevenueIntervalTarget} * 100 |\n      | Period-based output | {revenue} | {eligibleRevenuePtdOutputAchieved} |\n      | Interval/YTD output | {revenue} | {eligibleRevenueItdOutputAchieved} |\n      | Credit value | {dealSize} | {creditAmount} |\n      | Output of named measure | {outputAchieved} | {accessoriesRevenueBandDriverOutputAchieved} |\n      \n      PERCENT SCALE: If tiers use % values (e.g., \"0-80%\"), multiply by 100 for percentage scale.\n\n      CANONICAL VARIABLE-NAMING RULES:\n      - If the BRD says \"Output Achieved of <Measure Name>\", encode the measure name in the variable.\n      - Use camelCase measure hints plus IC semantic suffixes.\n      - Examples:\n        - {eligiblePrinterCreditAmountOutputAchieved}\n        - {accessoriesAttainmentDriverOutputAchieved}\n        - {accessoriesRevenueBandDriverOutputAchieved}\n        - {eligibleRevenueIntervalTarget}\n      - Only use bare generic variables such as {outputAchieved}, {ptdOutputAchieved}, or {itdOutputAchieved} when there is exactly one plausible measure source in scope.\n      - If two dimensions bind to different measures, the two inputExpression values MUST remain distinct.\n\n5. rateValues (array of rate row objects) - SAME LEVEL AS dimensions!\n   - Each payout has:\n     * coordinates: Dictionary mapping dimension names to values\n     * rate: Numeric payout rate (no symbols)\n     * confidence: Confidence in this payout value (0.0-1.0)\n\n6. confidence - Rate your confidence in this rate table extraction (0.0-1.0)\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n\nTIER VALIDATION:\n- Tiers must be in the EXACT order as presented in the document\n- Tiers must be NON-OVERLAPPING (tier 2 cannot start before tier 1 ends)\n- Tiers must be SEQUENTIAL with no gaps (if tier 1 ends at 100, tier 2 should start at 100)\n- Output exactly the number of tiers shown in document - no additions or omissions\n\nRANGE BOUNDARY PRESERVATION:\n- Preserve the exact interval semantics from the document\n- Only treat a range as open-ended when explicit indicators are present:\n  * \"1000+\" or \"1000-\" or \">1000\" or \"above 1000\" → open-ended\n  * \"1000-5000\" → finite range (preserve as \"1000-5000\")\n- Never convert large finite values to open-ended ranges\n- If document says \"$250,000 and above\", preserve that open-ended meaning\n- If dimensionType is RANGE, every entry in values[] must represent interval semantics (bounded or explicitly open-ended), not a discrete scalar point\n- Do NOT emit endpoint-only or scalar-only labels for RANGE dimensions\n- If the source wording does not support interval semantics with sufficient confidence, do not force a RANGE output; return ambiguity or omit the table instead of emitting malformed RANGE values\n- For numeric RANGE dimensions, normalize values[] for machine use:\n  * remove thousands separators\n  * remove currency symbols from the boundary text\n  * remove percent signs and comparative symbols from the stored boundary text\n  * keep interval structure\n  * example: `$4,000 - $8,000` -> `\"4000 - 8000\"`\n- For numeric RANGE dimensions, also emit normalized `tiers[]` with numeric bounds whenever confidence is sufficient\n\nGENERIC RANGE NORMALIZATION CONTRACT (CRITICAL):\n- Apply these rules to ANY numeric range wording, regardless of domain-specific labels.\n- For RANGE dimensions, every numeric band must be representable in BOTH forms:\n  1) normalized `values[]` interval label (string)\n  2) normalized `tiers[]` numeric bounds (numbers)\n- Normalize comparative language to interval semantics:\n  * \"X to Y\", \"between X and Y\", \"X - Y\" -> bounded interval\n  * \"above X\", \"> X\", \"X and above\", \"X+\" -> open-ended interval starting at X\n  * \"below Y\", \"< Y\", \"up to Y\" -> lower-bounded-from-zero interval when context supports numeric range scaling\n- Normalize number formatting consistently:\n  * strip commas, currency symbols, and percent symbols from numeric bounds\n  * expand shorthand numeric suffixes before storing bounds, for any upper- or lower-case suffix and for decimal values when present: `10K -> 10000`, `2.5M -> 2500000`, `10M -> 10000000`, `10B -> 10000000000`\n  * preserve sign and decimal precision where present\n- Canonical label guidance for `values[]`:\n  * EVERY numeric interval must be stored as `\"MIN - MAX\"` with numbers only\n  * never store `%`, `$`, `<`, `>`, `+`, `and above`, or other prose in `values[]`\n  * use a scale-appropriate far-limit numeric maximum when the source says `X+`, `> X`, or `X and above`\n  * ALWAYS expand shorthand first, then choose the far-limit from the expanded numeric scale; never choose the far-limit from the shorthand text itself\n  * that far-limit should be much larger than the explicit bounds in the same dimension and should look clearly open-ended for that scale\n  * choose an all-9s far-limit with at least 2-3 more digits than the largest explicit normalized bound in that dimension\n  * for low-hundreds / low-thousands scales, `999999` is acceptable; for million-scale bands use values such as `999999999`; for billion-scale bands use values such as `999999999999`\n  * use `0` as the canonical lower bound when the source says `< Y`, `below Y`, or `up to Y`\n  * examples:\n    - `90+` -> `\"90 - 999999\"` (small-scale example)\n    - `>90` -> `\"90 - 999999\"` (small-scale example)\n    - `<90` -> `\"0 - 90\"`\n    - `10M+` -> `\"10000000 - 999999999\"`\n    - `2.5M+` -> `\"2500000 - 999999999\"`\n    - `150%+` -> `\"150 - 999999\"` (small-scale example)\n- Shorthand-adaptive normalization rule:\n  * apply the same expansion and far-limit logic to ANY shorthand number, including `K`, `M`, `B`, `T`, mixed case, and decimal forms\n  * do not keep shorthand tokens such as `M` or `K` in persisted RANGE labels\n  * if one dimension uses million-scale numbers, do not fall back to `999999`; keep the open-ended maximum visibly above that scale\n- Coordinate parity requirement:\n  * each `rateValues[].coordinates[dimensionName]` MUST exactly match one normalized `values[]` entry\n  * do not emit coordinate labels that are prose-only variants of a normalized interval\n- If a numeric RANGE cannot be normalized with high confidence, do not guess:\n  * return no table for that ambiguous structure or use the ambiguity path instead of emitting unresolved RANGE output.\n\nGENERAL RULES:\n- Preserve the business meaning of dimension values.\n- LIST/TEXT values should preserve source wording closely.\n- RANGE values should prefer normalized machine-friendly interval text when numeric.\n- Rates should be numbers without percent signs or currency symbols\n- Preserve numeric rate magnitude exactly as written in the source:\n  - `2.5% -> 2.5`\n  - `1% -> 1`\n  - `0.01% -> 0.01`\n- Never convert percent values to ratio scale (e.g., do NOT convert `1%` to `0.01`)\n- Each unique combination of coordinates must have exactly ONE payout value\n- For 1D tables: Number of payout values = number of values in dimension\n- For 2D tables: Number of payout values = (dimension1 values) × (dimension2 values)\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON.\n- Strict JSON only (RFC 8259): no markdown, no code fences, no comments, no trailing commas.\n- All strings must use double quotes.\n- Every element in dimensions[].values[] MUST be a JSON string (double-quoted), even if it includes symbols.\n- If you are not 100% sure the output is valid JSON, return exactly: { \"rateTables\": [] }\n\n{\n  \"rateTables\": [\n    {\n      \"rateTableName\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"description\": \"string or null\",\n      \"rateTableType\": \"string (required) - exact code from LOOKUP CONTEXT commissionUnitAllowed\",\n      \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required)\",\n      \"dimensions\": [\n        {\n          \"dimensionName\": \"string (required, max 80 chars)\",\n          \"dimensionType\": \"RANGE | LIST | TEXT (required)\",\n          \"dimensionSequence\": \"1 | 2 (required)\",\n          \"unitOfMeasure\": \"string (required) - prefer LOOKUP CONTEXT commissionUnitAllowed; STRING and EXPRESSION also allowed when applicable\",\n          \"values\": [\"array of strings (required)\"],\n          \"tiers\": [\n            {\n              \"minimumAmount\": \"number or omitted\",\n              \"maximumAmount\": \"number or omitted\",\n              \"stringValue\": \"string or omitted\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"inputExpression\": \"string (required) - Variable e.g., {nrrRate}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rateValues\": [\n        {\n          \"coordinates\": { \"DimensionName\": \"value\" },\n          \"rate\": \"number (required)\",\n          \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0) (required)\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIMPORTANT REMINDERS:\n- rateValues must be at the SAME LEVEL as dimensions (NOT inside dimensions!)\n- Use {variable} format for inputExpression\n- Rates should be numbers without symbols\n- Coordinate keys must exactly match dimensionName values\n\nVARIABLE NAMING FOR inputExpression (CRITICAL):\n- The inputExpression variable should use a clear, canonical name that matches how formulas will reference this value\n- Example: If the rate table looks up based on \"combined weighted monthly revenue\", use {combinedRevenue} or {combinedWeightedRevenue}\n- If the input comes from a named measure result, include the measure name and semantic suffix in the variable\n- Avoid generic names like {value}, {input}, or bare {outputAchieved} when the component has multiple measures\n- This variable name will be used by the Expression Extractor and Expression Resolver to preserve the correct source binding\n\nRATE TABLE NAMING (CRITICAL):\n- Preserve the exact explicit table, scorecard, schedule, or lookup name from the source whenever one is stated\n- Do NOT rename multiple distinct tables in the same component to a single generic standardized name\n- If the source does not provide a clear explicit name, synthesize a descriptive fallback name that preserves the table's business role\n- The same business table must keep the same name across extraction and formula references\n\nSINGLE-BAND vs MARGINAL/PROGRESSIVE APPLICATION:\n- SINGLE-BAND: When text says \"the rate for that band applies to the ENTIRE amount\" or \"a single rate is applied to the whole figure\" - this means ONE rate multiplied by the full amount (e.g., {combinedRevenue} * RTR)\n- MARGINAL/PROGRESSIVE: When text says \"tiered rates\" or \"progressive\" or rates apply to \"amounts within each tier\" - this means different rates for different portions\n- If the document says \"the combined figure is compared to determine the applicable rate\" and then that rate is applied to the entire figure, this is SINGLE-BAND, not marginal\n- Default to SINGLE-BAND unless the document explicitly describes marginal/progressive calculation"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTables\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTableName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the rate table\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"description\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"What this table determines\"}, \"rateTableType\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PERCENT\", \"AMOUNT\"], \"description\": \"Type of rate values\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for rate table extraction\"}, \"dimensions\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"dimensionName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 80}, \"dimensionType\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"RANGE\", \"LIST\", \"TEXT\"]}, \"dimensionSequence\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 2}, \"unitOfMeasure\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"AMOUNT\", \"PERCENT\", \"STRING\", \"EXPRESSION\"]}, \"values\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"tiers\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"minimumAmount\": {\"type\": \"number\"}, \"maximumAmount\": {\"type\": \"number\"}, \"stringValue\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"inputExpression\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"dimensionName\", \"dimensionType\", \"dimensionSequence\", \"unitOfMeasure\", \"values\", \"inputExpression\"]}}, \"rateValues\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"coordinates\": {\"type\": \"object\"}, \"rate\": {\"type\": \"number\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0}}, \"required\": [\"coordinates\", \"rate\", \"confidence\"]}}}, \"required\": [\"rateTableName\", \"rateTableType\", \"confidence\", \"dimensions\", \"rateValues\"]}}}, \"required\": [\"rateTables\"]}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "code": "PC_EXPRESSION_EXTRACTOR",
                  "id": "1763096737017",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "PC Expression Extractor",
                    "reasoningEffort": "low",
                    "position": {
                      "x": 300,
                      "y": 400
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1763096850000"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "in_1763096737017_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert at analyzing compensation plan documents. Extract the component-level incentive formula for \"{{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\".\n\nCOMPONENT: {{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\n\nSLICED CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.SLICE_FOR_COMPONENT.$output.result}}\n\nSCOPE:\n\n- Extract COMPONENT incentive formula only (final payout calculation).\n- Do NOT extract measure formulas here (handled separately).\n- Do NOT decide scorecard vs component-level ownership here. RATE_TABLE_WIRING is authoritative for disambiguation.\n- Focus on the COMPONENT SECTION inside the SLICED CONTEXT for formula extraction. Use PLAN CONTEXT only for shared policy interpretation.\n\nINCENTIVE FORMULA CHARACTERISTICS:\n\n- Calculates final payout/bonus/commission amount for the component.\n- May reference measure outputs, target incentive, and/or RTR.\n- Represents the final component payout logic, not intermediate metric calculation.\n\nEXTRACTION RULES:\n\n1) Return one best candidate formula for this component.\n2) Prefer explicit formula definitions over examples.\n3) Keep the formula as one unit; do not split into sub-formulas.\n4) If uncertain, still return the best candidate with lower confidence and add an ambiguity entry.\n5) ALWAYS provide a business-friendly formula description.\n6) Treat `expression` as the best draft wording for the calculation intent, not the final canonical tokenized IC representation.\n\nFORMULA DESCRIPTION RULES:\n\n- `description` is required for every extracted incentive formula.\n- Write 1-2 concise business-facing sentences.\n- Explain what the component pays for and the high-level earning logic.\n- Use business language, not parser terminology or JSON field names.\n- Do not restate the formula token-by-token unless that detail is essential.\n- If the BRD is sparse, infer a reasonable business summary from the extracted formula and surrounding component context.\n\nRATE TABLE REFERENCES:\n\n- If the formula references a rate table (via RTR token), include names in `referencedRateTables`.\n- Use exact observed names from the document/extracted context; do not invent standardized names.\n\nEXPRESSION RULES:\n\n- Operators: *, /, +, -, ()\n- Variables: {variableName}\n- Rate lookup token: RTR\n- RTR must remain a bare token in formulas (`* RTR`). Do NOT output `RTR(...)` or `LOOKUP_RATETABLE(...)`.\n- TERMINAL LOOKUP INFERENCE:\n  - If the component-level rate table result is described as the final payout, bonus, commission, or component result, and no downstream arithmetic is described, you may infer a standalone lookup expression.\n  - A bare lookup alias such as `RTR` or `Rate Table Rate` is acceptable.\n  - Brief descriptive lookup phrasing is also acceptable when it clearly means only the standalone lookup result.\n  - Keep standalone lookup expressions concise and avoid long narrative prose in `expression`.\n  - Do not invent extra operands merely because a component-level rate table exists.\n  - If the document says the looked-up rate or multiplier is applied to revenue, output achieved, target incentive, or another operand, include that math explicitly (for example `{outputAchieved} * RTR`).\n  - If it is unclear whether the lookup result is final or only an intermediate factor, lower confidence and add ambiguity rather than forcing a standalone lookup expression.\n- Examples:\n  - If the BRD says the component payout schedule determines the final payout directly, `expression` may be a bare lookup alias or a concise standalone lookup phrase.\n  - If the BRD says the looked-up rate is applied to another operand, return the full math explicitly and do NOT collapse to a standalone lookup expression.\n- `variables` must include only operands explicitly referenced by the returned formula expression.\n- Do not include rate-table or scorecard driver attributes unless they appear directly in the expression itself.\n- If the expression is only a standalone rate-table lookup, return `variables: []`.\n- Keep `expression` concise and business-visible; do not try to emit final canonical tokens or low-level publish mechanics here.\n- Supported functions include CHOICE, IS_GREATER, IS_LESS, IS_EQUAL, IS_BETWEEN, SUM, NVL, LEAST, GREATEST, ROUND, NOT, AND, OR\n\nEVIDENCE RULES:\n\n- Include concise supporting snippet in `evidence`.\n- If confidence < 0.7, ambiguity entry is required.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON:\n\n{\n  \"formulas\": [\n    {\n      \"formulaName\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"expression\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"description\": \"string (required) - 1-2 business-friendly sentences explaining what payout this formula calculates\",\n      \"variables\": [\"array of strings\"],\n      \"referencedRateTables\": [\"array of strings\"],\n      \"source\": \"EXTRACTED\",\n      \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string (required)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"FORMULA_SELECTION | FORMULA_INCOMPLETE\",\n      \"message\": \"string\",\n      \"options\": [\"array of plausible alternatives\"],\n      \"confidence\": \"number (0.0-1.0)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n- `formulas` must contain exactly one item.\n- If ambiguity exists, still return one best-candidate formula and explain uncertainty in `ambiguities`.\n- Never return `null` or an empty string for `description`.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON with no markdown."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"formulas\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 1, \"description\": \"Exactly ONE incentive formula per component (1:1 mapping)\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"formulaName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the formula\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"expression\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Draft business-visible formula wording for resolver handoff, using {variables} where helpful\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Business-friendly summary of what this formula calculates\"}, \"variables\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"List of variable names used in the expression\"}, \"referencedRateTables\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Exact observed rate table names referenced by the draft formula wording\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet for the extracted incentive formula\"}, \"source\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"EXTRACTED\"], \"description\": \"Formula source - always EXTRACTED\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence score for formula extraction quality\"}}, \"required\": [\"formulaName\", \"expression\", \"description\", \"variables\", \"referencedRateTables\", \"evidence\", \"source\", \"confidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"ambiguities\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"type\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"FORMULA_SELECTION\", \"FORMULA_INCOMPLETE\"]}, \"message\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"options\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"type\", \"message\", \"options\", \"confidence\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}, \"required\": [\"formulas\", \"ambiguities\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "code": "RATE_TABLE_WIRING",
                  "id": "1763096850000",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Rate Table Wiring",
                    "reasoningEffort": "low",
                    "position": {
                      "x": 450,
                      "y": 250
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1763096851000"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "in_1763096850000_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert at analyzing Oracle Incentive Compensation (IC) plan structures. Your task is to determine how rate tables should be wired to measures and components, and infer IC configuration settings from BRD language.\n\nCOMPONENT: {{$context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_LOOP.$currentItem.componentName}}\n\nSLICED CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.SLICE_FOR_COMPONENT.$output.result}}\n\nEXTRACTED DATA FOR THIS COMPONENT:\n- Measures: {{$context.$nodes.PC_MEASURE_EXTRACTOR.$output}}\n- Rate Tables: {{$context.$nodes.RATE_TABLE_EXTRACTOR.$output}}\n- Incentive Formulas: {{$context.$nodes.PC_EXPRESSION_EXTRACTOR.$output}}\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n\nAnalyze the extracted rate tables and determine:\n1. How each rate table is USED (scorecard on measure vs component-level payout)\n2. What expressions feed each rate table dimension\n3. A business-friendly description for each rate-table input expression\n4. IC configuration settings (splitOption, splitFlag, accumulateFlag, firstTierAsThreshold)\n\nThis node is the AUTHORITATIVE disambiguation layer for rate table usage.\n\n=== PART 1: RATE TABLE USAGE ===\n\nSCORECARD (on measure):\n- Rate table attached to a MEASURE that helps determine the measure's result or a measure-owned driver feeding that result\n- Can take attainment, transaction attributes, quotas, credit amounts, quantities, or other business drivers as input\n- Can return a multiplier, scored amount, weighted result, attainment result, fixed amount, or other measure-level output\n- The rate-table lookup result is used WITHIN the measure or as a measure-owned lookup step before downstream calculations\n- A scorecard is not limited to attainment-percent patterns\n\nCOMPONENT_LEVEL (on component):\n- Rate table used in the component's INCENTIVE formula for final payout\n- Typically the last step before calculating payout amount\n- Example: \"Commission rate based on revenue tier\"\n\nUSAGE DETECTION RULES (in priority order):\n\nRULE 1: Check measure formula references\n- If a measure's formula.referencedRateTables[] contains a rate table name -> SCORECARD\n- The rate table transforms the measure's calculation\n\nRULE 2: Check incentive formula references  \n- If an incentive formula's referencedRateTables[] contains a rate table name -> COMPONENT_LEVEL\n- The rate table is used for final payout calculation\n\nRULE 3: Contextual analysis\n- If rate table is described in same section as a measure -> likely SCORECARD\n- If document says the table is attached to the measure, drives the measure, owns the input binding, or returns the measure result -> likely SCORECARD\n- If document says the lookup result itself becomes the final measure result with no further math -> likely SCORECARD with a terminal lookup measure formula\n- If document describes the table as an achievement scorecard, driver table, banding table, or lookup that converts an input into a measure output -> likely SCORECARD\n- If rate table is described as \"commission schedule\" or \"payout schedule\" -> likely COMPONENT_LEVEL\n- If document says the lookup result itself is the final component payout/bonus/commission with no further math -> likely COMPONENT_LEVEL with a terminal lookup incentive formula\n- If document describes using rate table output in further calculations -> SCORECARD\n- If document describes rate table as final step -> COMPONENT_LEVEL\n\n=== PART 2: DIMENSION INPUT EXPRESSIONS ===\n\nFor each rate table dimension, determine what value feeds into it.\n\nFor each dimension input assignment, also provide a concise business-friendly `description` that explains what business value the input expression represents.\n- Write 1-2 concise business-facing sentences.\n- Explain the driver in business terms, not parser or token internals.\n- Preserve named measure/component/attribute identity when it is known.\n- Example: \"Uses Activation Revenue Points output achieved PTD as the payout-schedule lookup driver.\"\n- Example: \"Uses credit amount to choose the correct commission band for each transaction.\"\n\nCOMMON INPUT PATTERNS:\n| Lookup Based On        | Input Expression                              |\n|------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| Attainment %           | {eligibleRevenueOutputAchieved} / {eligibleRevenueIntervalTarget} * 100 |\n| Revenue amount         | {creditAmount}                                |\n| Deal size              | {creditAmount}                                |\n| Named measure result   | {eligibleRevenueOutputAchieved}               |\n| Transaction attribute  | Credit.Credit Amount                          |\n\nCRITICAL RULES FOR INPUT EXPRESSIONS:\n1. Scorecard inputs can be either transaction attributes OR measure-result attributes, depending on BRD logic.\n2. Use measure-result inputs when BRD describes lookup by attainment/output (for example ITD Output Achieved).\n3. Use transaction-attribute inputs when BRD describes per-credit/deal amount lookup.\n4. Avoid circular references only when BRD clearly defines the same measure as both unresolved input and output in the same step.\n5. For COMPONENT_LEVEL rate tables, measure results are valid and common inputs.\n6. When a dimension is fed by a named measure result, preserve the measure identity in the variable name.\n7. Do NOT use bare generic variables such as {outputAchieved}, {ptdOutputAchieved}, or {itdOutputAchieved} when multiple measures are in scope.\n8. Good examples:\n   - {eligiblePrinterCreditAmountOutputAchieved}\n   - {accessoriesAttainmentDriverOutputAchieved}\n   - {accessoriesRevenueBandDriverOutputAchieved}\n9. Only use a bare generic achieved variable when there is exactly one plausible measure source in scope.\n10. Treat `inputExpression` as draft resolver input and visible business wording, not the final canonical tokenized expression contract.\n\n=== PART 3: IC CONFIGURATION INFERENCE ===\n\nFor each rate table, analyze the BRD to determine IC configuration settings.\n\n*** SPLIT OPTION (how attainment spans across tiers) ***\n\n| BRD Language | splitOption | Meaning |\n|--------------|-------------|---------|\n| \"interpolated\", \"sliding scale\", \"proportional rates\", \"pro-rated\" | PROPORTIONAL | Rate interpolated within tier |\n| \"X% increase per 1% attainment\", \"X% for every Y%\" | PROPORTIONAL | Incremental rate per unit |\n| \"step rates\", \"discrete tiers\", \"fixed rate per tier\", \"flat rate\" | NON_PROPORTIONAL | Rate applies to entire tier |\n| \"single rate\", \"one rate for whole amount\" | NONE | No tier splitting |\n| No clear indication | null | Cannot determine - leave null |\n\nIMPORTANT SPLIT OPTION GUARDRAIL:\n- Do NOT infer NON_PROPORTIONAL solely because a table has multiple tier rows.\n- If BRD does not explicitly describe split behavior, return splitOption=null.\n\n*** SPLIT DIMENSION (which dimension to split on) ***\n\n| Scenario | splitDimensionSequence | Confidence |\n|----------|------------------------|------------|\n| 1D rate table with splitOption set | 1 | HIGH (always 1 for 1D) |\n| 2D table, BRD says \"split on [dimension name]\" | Match to sequence | HIGH |\n| 2D table, one dimension is attainment/% based | That dimension | MEDIUM |\n| 2D table, cannot determine which dimension | Add SPLIT_DIMENSION ambiguity | - |\n\n*** ACCUMULATE FLAG (for scorecard inputs) ***\n\n| BRD Language | accumulateFlag | Confidence |\n|--------------|----------------|------------|\n| \"cumulative\", \"YTD\", \"year to date\", \"running total\", \"aggregate\" | true | HIGH |\n| \"per transaction\", \"each deal\", \"individual credit\", \"per credit\" | false | HIGH |\n| No clear indication | null | Cannot determine - leave null |\n\n*** FIRST TIER AS THRESHOLD ***\n\n| BRD Language | firstTierAsThreshold | Confidence |\n|--------------|---------------------|------------|\n| \"no payout until X%\", \"must reach X% before earning\" | true | HIGH |\n| \"0% rate from 0-X%\" with non-zero rate starting at X% | true | HIGH |\n| \"At X%: Y%\" as first non-zero entry (implying 0 before) | true | MEDIUM |\n| Tiers start with non-zero rate from 0% | false | HIGH |\n| No clear indication | null | Cannot determine - leave null |\n\nCONFIGURATION INFERENCE RULES:\n1. Only set values you can infer from the BRD - leave as null if no evidence\n2. For 1D tables, splitDimensionSequence is always 1 when splitOption is set\n3. For 2D tables where you cannot determine split dimension, add SPLIT_DIMENSION ambiguity\n4. splitOption applies at COMPONENT level; splitFlag is derived from splitDimensionSequence\n5. accumulateFlag only applies to SCORECARD usage (not COMPONENT_LEVEL)\n6. Keep splitOption null unless there is explicit BRD wording for split behavior.\n\n=== PART 4: AMBIGUITY HANDLING ===\n\nIf you cannot determine with high confidence (>0.7):\n- Add an ambiguity entry with type, message, options, confidence, evidence, and context identifiers\n- Options should be the plausible alternatives\n\nAmbiguity types:\n- USAGE_TYPE: Cannot determine if SCORECARD or COMPONENT_LEVEL\n- DIMENSION_INPUT: Cannot determine what feeds a dimension\n- RATE_TABLE_MATCH: Cannot match rate table to measure/formula\n- SPLIT_OPTION: Cannot determine if PROPORTIONAL, NON_PROPORTIONAL, or NONE\n- SPLIT_DIMENSION: For 2D tables, cannot determine which dimension to split on\n- ACCUMULATE_FLAG: Cannot determine if cumulative/YTD or per-transaction\n\n=== OUTPUT FORMAT ===\n\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON. No markdown, no code fences.\n\n{\n  \"rateTableAssignments\": [\n    {\n      \"rateTableName\": \"string (required) - exact name from extracted rate tables\",\n      \"usage\": \"SCORECARD | COMPONENT_LEVEL (required)\",\n      \"targetMeasure\": \"string or null - measure name if SCORECARD, null if COMPONENT_LEVEL\",\n      \"targetFormula\": \"string or null - formula name if COMPONENT_LEVEL, null if SCORECARD\", \n      \"confidence\": \"number 0.0-1.0 (required)\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"string - brief explanation of determination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string (required) - source snippet or extracted-data reference\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dimensionInputAssignments\": [\n    {\n      \"rateTableName\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"dimensionSequence\": \"integer 1-based (required)\",\n      \"dimensionName\": \"string (required, max 80 chars)\",\n      \"inputExpressionName\": \"string (required, max 80 chars) - final IC expression name for this dimensional input; no 'Input Expression' or 'Scorecard Input' prefix\",\n      \"description\": \"string (required) - 1-2 business-friendly sentences describing the input driver\",\n      \"inputExpression\": \"string (required) - IC-resolvable expression\",\n      \"confidence\": \"number 0.0-1.0 (required)\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"string - brief explanation\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string (required) - source snippet or extracted-data reference\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"configurationInferences\": [\n    {\n      \"rateTableName\": \"string (required) - exact name from extracted rate tables\",\n      \"splitOption\": \"PROPORTIONAL | NON_PROPORTIONAL | NONE | null\",\n      \"splitDimensionSequence\": \"integer 1 or 2, or null if cannot determine or splitOption is null\",\n      \"accumulateFlag\": \"boolean or null - only for SCORECARD usage\",\n      \"firstTierAsThreshold\": \"boolean or null\",\n      \"confidence\": \"number 0.0-1.0 (required)\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"string - brief explanation of how settings were inferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string (required) - source snippet or extracted-data reference\",\n      \"rateTransformation\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"USAGE_TYPE | DIMENSION_INPUT | RATE_TABLE_MATCH | SPLIT_OPTION | SPLIT_DIMENSION | ACCUMULATE_FLAG\",\n      \"rateTableName\": \"string (required)\",\n      \"dimensionName\": \"string or null - for DIMENSION_INPUT or SPLIT_DIMENSION type\",\n      \"dimensionSequence\": \"integer or null - when ambiguity is tied to a specific dimension sequence\",\n      \"targetMeasure\": \"string or null\",\n      \"targetFormula\": \"string or null\",\n      \"message\": \"string (required) - description of ambiguity\",\n      \"options\": [\"array of strings - plausible alternatives\"],\n      \"confidence\": \"number 0.0-1.0 (required)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"string (required)\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n- Process ALL rate tables in the extracted data\n- Every rate table must have an assignment (rateTableAssignments) OR an ambiguity entry\n- Every rate table must have a configurationInferences entry (even if all fields are null)\n- Every dimension must have an input assignment OR an ambiguity entry\n- Every dimension input assignment must include a non-empty `description`\n- Every dimension input assignment must include `inputExpressionName`, capped at 80 characters. Use a concise business name, optionally rate-table shorthand plus dimension name when that helps uniqueness. Do not prefix with \"Input Expression\" or \"Scorecard Input\".\n- Do not make assumptions - if unclear, add ambiguity or leave field as null\n- Use exact names from extracted data (rateTableName, dimensionName, measureName)\n- rateTransformation is always null (reserved for future use)\n- Keep reasoning concise; evidence is mandatory for all assignments and ambiguities"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTableAssignments\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"description\": \"Assignment of each rate table to its usage type and target\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTableName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Exact name of the rate table from extracted data\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"usage\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"SCORECARD\", \"COMPONENT_LEVEL\"], \"description\": \"How the rate table is used: SCORECARD (on measure) or COMPONENT_LEVEL (for final payout)\"}, \"targetMeasure\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Name of measure this scorecard is attached to (required if usage=SCORECARD)\"}, \"targetFormula\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Name of formula that uses this rate table (for COMPONENT_LEVEL)\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence in this assignment\"}, \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Brief explanation of how usage was determined\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet or extracted-data reference\"}}, \"required\": [\"rateTableName\", \"usage\", \"confidence\", \"reasoning\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"dimensionInputAssignments\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"description\": \"Input expression assignments for each rate table dimension\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTableName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the rate table\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"dimensionSequence\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 2, \"description\": \"1-based sequence number of the dimension\"}, \"dimensionName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 80, \"description\": \"Name of the dimension\"}, \"inputExpressionName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 80, \"description\": \"Final IC expression name for this rate dimensional input. Use the plan JSON value as the publisher expression Name.\"}, \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Business-friendly summary of what the dimensional input expression represents\"}, \"inputExpression\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Draft resolver input and business-visible expression wording that feeds this dimension (e.g., {creditAmount}, Credit.Credit Amount)\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence in this input expression\"}, \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Brief explanation of how input was determined\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet or extracted-data reference\"}}, \"required\": [\"rateTableName\", \"dimensionSequence\", \"dimensionName\", \"inputExpressionName\", \"description\", \"inputExpression\", \"confidence\", \"reasoning\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"configurationInferences\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"description\": \"IC configuration settings inferred from BRD language for each rate table\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"rateTableName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Exact name of the rate table\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"splitOption\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"PROPORTIONAL\", \"NON_PROPORTIONAL\", \"NONE\", null], \"description\": \"How attainment is split across rate tiers. PROPORTIONAL=interpolated within tier, NON_PROPORTIONAL=step rates, NONE=single rate\"}, \"splitDimensionSequence\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 2, \"description\": \"Which dimension to split on (1 or 2). For 1D tables, always 1 when splitOption is set.\"}, \"accumulateFlag\": {\"type\": [\"boolean\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Whether to use cumulative/YTD values for scorecard lookup. true=YTD/cumulative, false=per transaction\"}, \"firstTierAsThreshold\": {\"type\": [\"boolean\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Whether first tier acts as threshold (no payout until met). true=threshold behavior\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence in these inferences\"}, \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Brief explanation of how settings were inferred from BRD\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet or extracted-data reference\"}, \"rateTransformation\": {\"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"RESERVED for Phase B - rate value transformation metadata (e.g., incremental to total conversion)\"}}, \"required\": [\"rateTableName\", \"confidence\", \"reasoning\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"ambiguities\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"description\": \"Ambiguities that could not be resolved with high confidence (<70%)\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"type\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"USAGE_TYPE\", \"DIMENSION_INPUT\", \"RATE_TABLE_MATCH\", \"SPLIT_OPTION\", \"SPLIT_DIMENSION\", \"ACCUMULATE_FLAG\"], \"description\": \"Type of ambiguity\"}, \"rateTableName\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Name of the rate table with ambiguity\"}, \"dimensionName\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Name of the dimension (for DIMENSION_INPUT or SPLIT_DIMENSION type)\"}, \"dimensionSequence\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 2, \"description\": \"Dimension sequence when ambiguity is tied to a specific dimension\"}, \"targetMeasure\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Candidate measure involved in the ambiguity, if applicable\"}, \"targetFormula\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Candidate formula involved in the ambiguity, if applicable\"}, \"message\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Human-readable description of the ambiguity\"}, \"options\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Plausible alternatives for resolution\"}, \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0.0, \"maximum\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Confidence for this ambiguity assessment\"}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"Supporting source snippet or extracted-data reference\"}}, \"required\": [\"type\", \"rateTableName\", \"message\", \"options\", \"confidence\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}, \"required\": [\"rateTableAssignments\", \"dimensionInputAssignments\", \"configurationInferences\", \"ambiguities\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "CODE",
                  "code": "BUNDLE_LOOP_OUTPUT",
                  "id": "1763096851000",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Bundle Loop Output",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "position": {
                      "x": 550,
                      "y": 250
                    },
                    "sourceCode": "// BUNDLE_LOOP_OUTPUT - Plan Builder CODE node\n//\n// Bundles loop extractor outputs with rate table wiring output.\n// Output shape matches the assembler expectation:\n// {\"0\": componentDetail, \"1\": measures, \"2\": rateTables, \"3\": formulas, \"4\": wiring}\n\nvar result = new Object();\n\nvar c0 = $context.$nodes.PLAN_COMPONENT_DETAIL_EXTRACTOR.$output;\nvar c1 = $context.$nodes.PC_MEASURE_EXTRACTOR.$output;\nvar c2 = $context.$nodes.RATE_TABLE_EXTRACTOR.$output;\nvar c3 = $context.$nodes.PC_EXPRESSION_EXTRACTOR.$output;\nvar c4 = $context.$nodes.RATE_TABLE_WIRING.$output;\n\nresult[\"0\"] = new Object();\nresult[\"0\"].content = typeof c0 === 'string' ? c0 : JSON.stringify(c0);\n\nresult[\"1\"] = new Object();\nresult[\"1\"].content = typeof c1 === 'string' ? c1 : JSON.stringify(c1);\n\nresult[\"2\"] = new Object();\nresult[\"2\"].content = typeof c2 === 'string' ? c2 : JSON.stringify(c2);\n\nresult[\"3\"] = new Object();\nresult[\"3\"].content = typeof c3 === 'string' ? c3 : JSON.stringify(c3);\n\nresult[\"4\"] = new Object();\nresult[\"4\"].content = typeof c4 === 'string' ? c4 : JSON.stringify(c4);\n\nreturn result;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1763095839856"
                  },
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
